I love being anywhere near the water  especially during the summer I heard  from friends that Muskoka is Canada's  version of the Hamptons and I really  wanted to see it for myself the view  from my hotel was unreal there's all  these lakes and different waterways and  things that are all linked together and  different landscapes surrounding them  that you can see pretty much everywhere  you turn it's one of the most beautiful  areas in Canada with all the rocks the  islands fishing is pretty popular here  so I had a local guy take me out on his  boat highlight of that experience was  definitely catching a bass for the first  time poor calling the downtown area has  all of these amazing restaurants and  authentic shops where I've met my  friends after with Toronto being only  two hours away it has a really diverse  crowd I was really excited that my  fiance was able to meet me for the  weekend made it having her there to  experience it with me just made it that  much better  [Music]  Ontario is extremely close to home but  it's completely different than anything  we have in the States it's beautiful and  it feels miles away from a big city go  and wakeboarding on the lakes there made  me really feel like I was one of the  locals  if you just want to get away and have a  blast and thus coca is definitely the  place  [Music]  I would do this trip all over again in a  heartbeat  [Music]
 

